1: # Marked infinity source, Cartier line, caps, and collision periods
2: 
3: This working note records actual maps for the infinity puncture of the marked
4: source cover. It assigns no completed-family return. The literal collision
5: quotient, its attachment to the cap and selected-cusp trace, and their oriented
6: boundary remain separate maps to be supplied. The calculations use the source,
7: divisor lines, and primitive chord lift already fixed in K39's working note.
8: 
9: ## IF.1. The marked infinity chart and selected-node units
10: 
11: On the cover \(\rho^2=1+v\), put \(\epsilon=\rho^{-1}\). The source map is
12: \[
13:  v=\epsilon^{-2}-1,\qquad
14:  X=\epsilon^{-2}x,\quad Y=\epsilon^{-3}y,\quad T=\epsilon^{-4}t.
15: \]
16: It carries the actual marked equation and section to
17: \[
18:  y^2=x^3+(-2+3\epsilon^2)x^2+t x
19:                      +\epsilon^2(1-\epsilon^2)^2,\qquad
20:  G=(0,g),\quad g=\epsilon(1-\epsilon^2).                 \tag{IF.1}
21: \]
22: Write \(A=1-\epsilon^2\), \(t_*=A(1-3\epsilon^2)\), and \(q_*=t-t_*\).
23: The selected fibre factors and normalizes by the literal formulas
24: \[
